@nsobid-646761F643AFEBB379EDD5E6A5151AF2CEF93DC1

# Metroid Dread 2.1.0 - Full resolution shadows

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders gameplay shadow maps at the full resolution cutscenes use.
//
// Every frame the shadow pass (sub_7100211590) picks how much of each shadow
// map a light may use: 0.25 in gameplay and 1.0 in cinematics (unless the
// cutscene opts out). That factor is stored twice: once as the viewport scale
// the light is rendered with (sub_7100210A04) and once in the per-light
// shader data next to the map's texel size (sub_71001CEF80), so the depth
// render and the sampling stay in agreement. In gameplay a 2048x2048 map is
// therefore only drawn into a 512x512 corner.
//
// Both writes of the 0.25 constant become 1.0, so gameplay and every cutscene
// use the whole map. Lights flagged to ignore the factor are unaffected.
//
// Costs about 16x the shadow-map fill for those lights. Stacks with
// [Shadow Resolution 4096], which then gives 4096x4096 in gameplay too.

@enabled
00211868 08F0A752   // MOVZ W8,#0x3F80,LSL#16 = 1.0f (was 0.25f, gameplay scale)
002118A0 08F0A752   // MOVZ W8,#0x3F80,LSL#16 = 1.0f (was 0.25f, cutscene opt-out)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Metroid Dread 2.1.0 (MercurySteam engine,
// NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
